__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.step
*.stl
_studio_mesh.stl
*.tcad.json
# the design LIBRARY is user work — back it up (root-level .tcad.json are
# self-test artifacts and stay ignored)
!designs/*.tcad.json
# uploaded import files are user work too: designs reference them by name,
# so a backup without them would not rebuild
!imports/*.stl
# frozen design copies the code tests read (LAUNCH-PLAN.md R6) — must travel
# with the code or a fresh clone's suite is red
!tests/fixtures/*.tcad.json
# the bug inbox (LAUNCH-PLAN.md P5b): tests/journeys.py and the Studio bug
# button save a design copy + the failing request per folder. Tracked so a
# repro survives to the chat that fixes it; that chat deletes the folder.
!bugs/**
# ... except the runner's own run log, which grows every night
bugs/journeys.log
# ... and the kernel worker's own record of every crash and stopped call it
# turned into a sentence (kernelguard.py). It is a LOG, appended to for ever
# by every run; the findings that matter become bug folders and plan rows.
bugs/kernel-crashes.log

# Version histories are user work too (VERSION-TREE-PLAN.md): designs/<slug>.history/
# holds index.json + gzipped snapshots, ~10 KB each. User's call 2026-08-26:
# TRACK them, same reasoning as the design library above — losing v1..v9 to an
# untracked directory would defeat the point of recording them. Nothing here
# matches those names today; the explicit rule keeps it that way if a broader
# *.json ignore ever lands.
!designs/*.history/**
.studio-session.json
.studio-session.tmp
.studio-session-*.json

# lint tooling (CLAUDE.md, Commands): ESLint's packages install locally, never committed
.claude/lint/node_modules/
.claude/lint/package-lock.json
.ruff_cache/

# probe scratch: bodies and timings written by probes/sidecar_*.py
probes/_sidecar_tmp/

# Claude's own scratch, and the trap that caught a `git add -A` on 2026-09-16:
# a worktree is an embedded git repo, so it commits as a gitlink and takes a
# peer session's in-progress tree with it. probes/_*.brep is NOT here on
# purpose — a crash body kept as a repro is meant to be committed.
.claude/worktrees/
.playwright-mcp/
